# The fleet installer's ingredients — the ONE place the Talos version and
# the official system extensions are spelled out. build.sh sources this;
# talos/hardware/*.yaml pin the image it produces (tag + digest) and point
# here rather than repeating the list. Bump Talos or an extension here,
# rebuild BOTH variants, repin all four hardware files (minipc and
# terramaster the plain image; alienware-x15 and asus-tuf-b550-pro the
# `-nvidia` one).
#
# Refs: https://factory.talos.dev/version/$TALOS/extensions/official
# (iscsi-tools + util-linux-tools are Longhorn's, ADR-0011. nebula
# 1.10.3 rode here from factory schematic 6a9acc… until Mesh v3 Phase 4
# P4.1 dropped it, 2026-09-21: the identity plane carries everything.
# kata-containers is the sandbox layer for agent workloads — spike
# bog2, decision 6d0u: registers the `kata` (cloud-hypervisor) and
# `kata-qemu` containerd handlers; k8s/apps/sandbox/ declares the
# RuntimeClass.)
TALOS=v1.12.6
#
# EVERY ref carries the digest the Image Factory lists for THIS Talos
# version (the URL above returns ref + digest per extension) — a bare
# tag is not a pin. Sidero rebuilds extensions for each Talos release
# under the SAME tag: on 2026-11-17 `iscsi-tools:v0.2.0` resolved to a
# build linked against libcrypto.so.4, v1.12.6's rootfs has .so.3, and
# a by-tag rebuild of this installer booted w1 with ext-iscsid in a
# crash loop and Longhorn down on the node until `talosctl rollback`
# (kata-containers and nvidia-container-toolkit-lts had moved too).
# build.sh refuses a ref without @sha256. Bumping TALOS means
# re-reading every digest from the factory list for the new version.
OFFICIAL=(
  ghcr.io/siderolabs/iscsi-tools:v0.2.0@sha256:b30127b2f3ea6a49aa73dcf18c30da1fa1d2604da00c60519f8f00b4c6d25294
  ghcr.io/siderolabs/util-linux-tools:2.41.2@sha256:8433604b21ec56871b00f363008ab455b2ece264246be915a2d6f742ec90ffcb
  ghcr.io/siderolabs/kata-containers:3.26.0@sha256:418b5fed37ed6388104c1f624ad7a0e9b65b0578f7d7d30b7dbce676f5d5394a
)
# GPU nodes only (w1, w2 — epic talos-config-e6rx; the owner ruled
# "only the GPU nodes", so the fleet runs TWO images that differ by
# exactly this list). `VARIANT=nvidia build.sh --installer-only` appends
# it and tags the result `…-$SUFFIX-nvidia`.
# - The OPEN kernel modules, not nonfree-kmod-nvidia: the installer is
#   a public ghcr image (ADR-0023) and both cards are Ampere, which the
#   open modules support.
# - The `lts` pair, not `production`: lts is the 580 branch, production
#   is 570, and the CUDA 13 userspace in the cu130 PyTorch wheels
#   (comfyui/versions.env) needs a 580+ driver.
# The kmod tag carries the Talos version it was built against — bump it
# with TALOS. Loading the modules is per machine (kernel.modules in the
# two hardware files); the extensions alone bind nothing.
NVIDIA=(
  ghcr.io/siderolabs/nvidia-open-gpu-kernel-modules-lts:580.126.20-v1.12.6@sha256:fd88db1ec64377803d34694397b75d8e8b266fcceb4a0f79bc559af359b080b8
  ghcr.io/siderolabs/nvidia-container-toolkit-lts:580.126.20-v1.18.2@sha256:c2637813917dcacdb5838e3f38467a3646f35aad9b12cf09447875318f9c5ce5
)
# Installer tag suffix after `<talos>-p0agent-<ver>`: bump when the
# OFFICIAL list changes without a p0agent release, so two installers
# with different contents never share a tag (the digest is the pin,
# ADR-0023, but a tag that lies is still a trap). Empty = none.
SUFFIX=kata
